    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "405f72c5132757b1b82a15fc3094fadcde96e278afcc9a5f8c8cbb6a398d7c92",
      "text": "Buenos Aires – Iguazu. Full-day excursion to the Argentine side of the Iguazu Falls, where trails and walkways lead through the rainforest of a 55,500-hectare national park and bring you remarkably close to the waterfalls. The visit includes three main circuits.\n\nLower Circuit · A 1,700-metre jungle trail passes waterfalls such as Dos Hermanas, Chico and Ramírez and reaches the foot of the impressive Salto Bossetti, with close views of the Álvar Núñez, Elenita and Lanusse falls.\n\nUpper Circuit · A 1,300-metre elevated walkway follows the upper edge of several major waterfalls, offering panoramic views across the surrounding landscape.\n\nDevil’s Throat · The ecological train runs through the rainforest to Devil’s Throat Station, where a 1,000-metre walkway leads to the immense Devil’s Throat and the full power of the water at close range.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_aligned",
        "fileId": "1tL8rORSfz4CoqnMwj7pS8zoSc7bwa57M",
        "documentSha256": "ab68209110fffc145b516391bf0e33879712ea1e9d30e68f1f8f3d33a06bc487",
        "paragraphs": [
